# Local machine facts

<!-- Customize for your environment. Copy to ~/.claude/local.md (never into a repository), fill in measured values,
     delete sections that do not apply, then run bin/kb sync-agents. Shared rules say "see local.md" for everything below. -->

## Machine

- OS: <measured, e.g. from skills/research-setup/scripts/hardware>
- Logical CPUs: <measured>
- Memory: <measured total>; swap: <measured>
- GPU: <present / none; do not guess>
- Package manager: <e.g. Homebrew or mise (user-level), or apt only with passwordless sudo>
- Install location: <e.g. ~/.local/bin, ~/.local/opt, or the Homebrew prefix>
- Passwordless sudo: <yes / no; if no, write commands that need sudo for the user to run>
- Install log: <default ~/.config/research/installs.log>

## Time

- Report times in: <your timezone, e.g. UTC or Europe/Berlin>. Machine clock is in: <its timezone, if different>.
- To get the current time in your zone: <command, e.g. TZ=<zone> date>

## Concurrency and resources

- Memory measure that gates parallel tests, builds and browsers: <recommended: real anonymous memory of your user, not "available" memory that includes reclaimable cache>
  - Linux with cgroup v2: the `anon` line of `/sys/fs/cgroup/<your user slice>/memory.stat`; macOS: "App Memory" in Activity Monitor or `vm_stat`.
  - Throttle new parallel work above <about 50-60% of your memory limit>; your user is throttled at <limit> and killed at <limit>, if a limit exists.
- Read-only delegation has no fixed fan-out; each extra agent session costs about <measured MB>.
- Build parallelism: <e.g. -j<N>; recommended: about half the logical CPUs, fewer on a shared machine>. Lower priority for builds and tests: <e.g. nice -n 10>.
- Long commands get a timeout: <default seconds>.
- Services not to touch: <names, e.g. a proxy or VPN you depend on>.
- Process hygiene: kill by PID after checking start time (`ps -eo pid,etime,args`); avoid pattern kills that can match your own shell.
- Scheduled jobs: <none / list the jobs that exist on purpose, e.g. the weekly rules sync>.

## Files and storage

- Must survive a restart or another day (evidence, screenshots, artifacts): the task directory.
- Intermediate files during a session: <session scratch directory, or /tmp>; delete when the session ends. Shared scratch: delete only what you created.
- Read once and discard: /tmp.
- User-level software: <e.g. ~/.local/bin>; language runtimes: <version manager>; project dependencies: <per-project virtual environment>; global tools may be installed, but log them (see "Installing software" in the executor conventions).

## Browser checks

- Tool: <one per platform; Linux/headless: a CLI browser-automation tool driving a local Chrome or Chromium; macOS: a desktop browser agent or the same CLI tool>
- Setup: <executable path, socket or profile directory, headless or not>
- Notes: <e.g. no GPU, so WebGL is slow; measure frame rate on real hardware>

## Notifications and boards

- How a Lead reaches the dispatcher: <built-in cross-session messaging / herdr agent prompt / STATUS only>
- How the dispatcher reaches the user: <terminal / app notification / phone push / none>
- Board: <local BOARD.md / Notion (credentials in ~/.config/research/notion.env)>

## Accounts and transfers

- Git hosting CLI: <e.g. gh, logged in as your account>
- File exchange with your other devices: <inbox/outbox directories or none>

## Roles

Do not list models here. Copy `templates/roles.toml.example` to `~/.config/research/roles.toml`, edit it, and run `bin/models`; it writes `~/.config/research/models.md`, which `bin/kb sync-agents` appends after this file.
